This app renders video with, and depends on (npm, unmodified):

- HyperFrames (https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright HeyGen. It turns the HTML compositions the app writes (captions, title card,
  pictures over the video, shorts, thumbnail) into video and pictures with Chrome.
  The Apache License 2.0 text: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

- GSAP (https://gsap.com), the animation library HyperFrames compositions are timed with,
  under GSAP's Standard "no charge" license: https://gsap.com/standard-license

It calls these programs, which are not part of it and are installed separately:
- ffmpeg and ffprobe (https://ffmpeg.org), for cutting, sound and encoding.
- yt-dlp (https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp), optional, for YouTube and similar links.

No speech or language model is bundled or downloaded: transcription and writing use the
services the person sets in Settings.
